00:16:16,341 --> 00:16:17,021
Trust me.

264
00:16:18,501 --> 00:16:21,661
For what it's worth, I seriously hate your guts, too.

265
00:16:22,441 --> 00:16:23,481
But besides all that,

266
00:16:23,961 --> 00:16:26,361
the only thing I hate even more than seeing your dumb face

267
00:16:26,361 --> 00:16:28,141
is knowing that you're the only one

268
00:16:28,141 --> 00:16:29,801
who can truly intimidate Kaneda.

269
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:32,761
Okay.

270
00:16:34,801 --> 00:16:36,541
I'm putting my trust in you.

271
00:16:42,541 --> 00:16:44,421
Center backs who aren't even in sync,

272
00:16:44,501 --> 00:16:45,841
don't scare me one bit!

273
00:16:47,021 --> 00:16:48,661
Think you can stop me, punk?

274
00:16:48,661 --> 00:17:07,181
What the heck happened during halftime?

275
00:17:12,121 --> 00:17:12,821
Got it!

276
00:17:14,701 --> 00:17:15,561
Hey, you idiot!

277
00:17:15,801 --> 00:17:17,361
Don't let yourself get pincered!

278
00:17:17,361 --> 00:17:28,621
Kick it out!

279
00:17:32,201 --> 00:17:33,501
Come on, right now?

280
00:17:33,741 --> 00:17:35,181
We were in a good position!

281
00:17:39,061 --> 00:17:40,341
Dust off your empathy

282
00:17:40,341 --> 00:17:42,861
and try to understand each other.

283
00:17:42,861 --> 00:17:47,141
There's something Aoi said

284
00:17:47,141 --> 00:17:49,481
that has stayed with me more than anything else.

285
00:17:49,621 --> 00:17:49,921
What?

286
00:17:51,561 --> 00:17:54,521
He said I should try to understand you more.

287
00:17:54,661 --> 00:17:56,281
So I did, and...

288
00:17:56,281 --> 00:17:56,521
Oh!

289
00:17:57,801 --> 00:17:59,681
I realized you're unique.

290
00:18:00,561 --> 00:18:03,141
Out of all the center backs I've partnered with,

291
00:18:03,261 --> 00:18:03,781
you...

292
00:18:03,781 --> 00:18:04,861
you gotta be...

293
00:18:04,861 --> 00:18:05,601
Oh!

294
00:18:05,601 --> 00:18:09,881
The dumbest, stupidest ass!

295
00:18:14,041 --> 00:18:14,561
Kurira!

296
00:18:16,361 --> 00:18:17,661
The way you play,

297
00:18:18,441 --> 00:18:20,721
every movement has a point, right?

298
00:18:20,721 --> 00:18:23,321
It's obvious enough just from watching.

299
00:18:24,181 --> 00:18:27,181
You don't make a move unless there's logic behind it.

300
00:18:28,981 --> 00:18:30,661
Pretty sure I play like everyone.

301
00:18:30,661 --> 00:18:32,741
Yeah, I know.

302
00:18:33,041 --> 00:18:34,841
You take it to the extreme, my friend.

303
00:18:35,001 --> 00:18:36,361
You're such a logic fiend.

304
00:18:40,361 --> 00:18:42,421
And you were like that even as a kid.

305
00:18:43,181 --> 00:18:43,681
Unwavering.

306
00:18:44,461 --> 00:18:45,621
That's really something.

307
00:18:49,621 --> 00:18:50,101
Hey!

308
00:18:50,261 --> 00:18:51,041
We're restarting.

309
00:18:51,181 --> 00:18:52,861
Better make sure you guys hydrate.

310
00:18:52,861 --> 00:18:58,581
I hope you realize

311
00:18:58,581 --> 00:19:00,621
this doesn't mean we're friends now, Togashi.

312
00:19:01,401 --> 00:19:03,701
You're the kind of dude that I ding-dong ditch.

313
00:19:03,881 --> 00:19:05,241
You're lucky I don't know where you live.

314
00:19:18,821 --> 00:19:19,261
Unwavering.

315
00:19:19,681 --> 00:19:21,341
That's you too, Togashi.

316
00:19:21,341 --> 00:19:29,801
Oh, you little shit!

317
00:19:30,461 --> 00:19:32,501
What the heck are they doing?

318
00:19:32,781 --> 00:19:33,741
Who goes after a ball

319
00:19:33,741 --> 00:19:35,341
that's been thrown back in after an injury?

320
00:19:42,761 --> 00:19:43,721
To the wing?

321
00:19:44,441 --> 00:19:45,001
Damn it.

322
00:19:45,241 --> 00:19:45,781
Damn you!

323
00:19:45,781 --> 00:19:45,841
Damn you!

324
00:19:45,841 --> 00:19:58,241
Well, well, Kaneda.

325
00:19:58,801 --> 00:20:00,201
I knew that you'd run.

326
00:20:03,141 --> 00:20:06,181
Thankfully, you ran right where I expected you to.

327
00:20:06,421 --> 00:20:06,801
What?

328
00:20:06,801 --> 00:20:11,221
You guys, it isn't against the rules

329
00:20:11,221 --> 00:20:13,141
to go after a ball that's been given back.

330
00:20:13,441 --> 00:20:14,341
But that conduct was...

331
00:20:14,341 --> 00:20:15,181
Shut up, all right?

332
00:20:15,221 --> 00:20:16,101
I know what happened.

333
00:20:20,861 --> 00:20:21,261
Kaneda.

334
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:24,401
I had a lot of respect for you until halftime.

335
00:20:24,981 --> 00:20:26,761
But now, it's like you went back.

336
00:20:27,381 --> 00:20:29,041
You're the same as you were last year.

337
00:20:29,541 --> 00:20:30,101
What?

338
00:20:30,101 --> 00:20:32,381
So step off!

339
00:20:32,381 --> 00:20:34,001
Because it's our turn now!

340
00:20:35,001 --> 00:20:36,341
Do your best.

341
00:20:36,761 --> 00:20:37,481
Don't lose.

342
00:20:38,141 --> 00:20:39,601
Fight to your limits.

343
00:20:39,601 --> 00:20:43,961
Keep calm!

344
00:20:44,261 --> 00:20:45,261
Forget the highline!

345
00:20:45,521 --> 00:20:46,581
And stand your ground!

346
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,081
Watch out for the defense.

347
00:20:52,461 --> 00:20:53,541
The defense.

348
00:20:54,361 --> 00:20:56,401
With Togashi, Takashima, and Kurata

349
00:20:56,401 --> 00:20:57,681
working as a unit now,

350
00:20:58,341 --> 00:21:00,221
all I really have to do is support them.

351
00:21:01,341 --> 00:21:02,541
I'm not saying that

352
00:21:02,541 --> 00:21:03,941
because I want to go on the attack.

353
00:21:04,541 --> 00:21:05,661
It's just...

354
00:21:05,661 --> 00:21:07,641
That is how strong they are together.

355
00:21:08,201 --> 00:21:09,441
Which means next up.

356
00:21:13,921 --> 00:21:14,441
Asari.

357
00:21:16,721 --> 00:21:17,321
Damn.

358
00:21:17,761 --> 00:21:18,601
They've all pulled back

359
00:21:18,601 --> 00:21:19,941
and they're really compact now.

360
00:21:20,641 --> 00:21:21,161
Segurata!

361
00:21:24,441 --> 00:21:25,501
Are you kidding?

362
00:21:25,881 --> 00:21:27,361
All of them have dropped back.

363
00:21:27,941 --> 00:21:28,881
So what should I do?

364
00:21:30,721 --> 00:21:31,241
Huh?

365
00:21:31,661 --> 00:21:31,961
Oh.

366
00:21:33,941 --> 00:21:37,041
Both fullbacks are...

367
00:21:37,041 --> 00:21:38,541
They've pushed all the way up

368
00:21:38,541 --> 00:21:39,581
on both wings.

369
00:21:39,841 --> 00:21:40,801
Are they mocking us?

370
00:21:41,341 --> 00:21:42,261
Both their fullbacks

371
00:21:42,261 --> 00:21:43,101
have totally abandoned

372
00:21:43,101 --> 00:21:44,001
the defensive line.

373
00:21:44,441 --> 00:21:45,501
This is the perfect time

374
00:21:45,501 --> 00:21:46,861
to pass me the damn ball!

375
00:21:51,861 --> 00:21:52,341
Damn.

376
00:21:52,761 --> 00:21:53,841
I haven't had this view

377
00:21:53,841 --> 00:21:55,001
of the field in a while.

378
00:21:55,661 --> 00:21:56,481
Oh, man.

379
00:21:57,101 --> 00:21:58,021
It's nice.

380
00:21:59,181 --> 00:22:00,421
What's that guy's problem?

381
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:02,301
Why is he looking at us like that?

382
00:22:02,301 --> 00:22:04,661
I'm gonna go mark the creepy kid.

383
00:22:04,941 --> 00:22:06,301
You all stay right where you are!

384
00:22:10,401 --> 00:22:10,841
Stagnation.

385
00:22:12,941 --> 00:22:13,381
Stagnation.

386
00:22:13,901 --> 00:22:14,981
I like that word.

387
00:22:15,601 --> 00:22:17,401
It's all starting to make sense now.

388
00:22:17,401 --> 00:22:25,861
It's just like at the tryouts

389
00:22:25,861 --> 00:22:27,121
and in the Sekio match.

390
00:22:27,781 --> 00:22:28,181
No.

391
00:22:28,901 --> 00:22:30,381
It's more vivid and clearer

392
00:22:30,381 --> 00:22:31,341
than it was before.

393
00:22:32,041 --> 00:22:32,961
It's wild.

394
00:22:34,961 --> 00:22:36,381
This guy's got it coming.

395
00:22:37,061 --> 00:22:38,781
I'll show him how useless it is

396
00:22:38,781 --> 00:22:40,041
for a fullback to push up

397
00:22:40,041 --> 00:22:40,721
without a plan.

398
00:22:40,721 --> 00:22:46,761
Stagnation.

399
00:22:47,261 --> 00:22:47,861
Stagnation.

400
00:22:48,461 --> 00:22:49,101
Stagnation.

401
00:22:49,601 --> 00:22:50,341
Stagnation.

402
00:22:50,341 --> 00:22:50,421
Stagnation.

403
00:22:53,221 --> 00:22:54,881
Has your perspective changed?

404
00:22:55,281 --> 00:22:56,561
What do your eyes see now?

405
00:22:57,041 --> 00:22:58,261
They're far more sophisticated

406
00:22:58,261 --> 00:22:59,581
than they were back then

407
00:22:59,581 --> 00:23:01,021
during the Sekio match.

408
00:23:01,701 --> 00:23:02,681
Think about it

409
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:03,521
over and over

410
00:23:03,521 --> 00:23:04,261
and then

411
00:23:04,261 --> 00:23:05,981
